  "status": "implemented-source-derived-symbolic-plus-conservative-s4-aliases",
  "methodology": [
    "Each native code family is a real standalone CosmWasm contract with concrete storage semantics.",
    "Each symbolic artifact was derived from the complete checked-in native source and records the source SHA-256 plus line-scoped evidence.",
    "Historical Ethereum concrete read/write keys are forbidden as symbolic-analysis inputs and are not embedded in these contracts or artifacts.",
    "Candidate extension families are workload analogues for the observed selector semantics; they are not claims of byte-for-byte Ethereum application equivalence.",
    "S1 extends the reusable native family registry with selector-reviewed cw721-drop and stargate-cw20 families; unreviewed selectors remain explicit fallbacks and are excluded from selector-aware conflict coverage.",
    "S4 adds custom-swap-router as an independent storage namespace reusing the checked-in marketplace-router CosmWasm binary/profile only for a conservative singleton route-execution guard; this is explicitly not an application-equivalence claim.",
    "S4 adds v3-pool-lock as an independent per-pool storage namespace reusing the marketplace-router singleton ExecuteRoute dependency guard for the observed Uniswap-V3 swap class; ticks, liquidity math, settlement, and EVM execution equivalence are intentionally out of scope.",
    "S4 fourth-batch review adds distinct amp-partition-collateral-lock, linea-rollup-lock, zksync-l1-system-lock, and arbitrum-bridge-lock namespaces. Each reuses only the checked-in marketplace-router ExecuteRoute singleton dependency guard as a conservative per-source-owner lock; public-source evidence is checked in separately and no EVM state/execution equivalence is claimed.",
    "S4 fifth-batch review adds synthetix-system-lock and starknet-l1-system-lock as distinct conservative per-owner dependency aliases. Generic proxy runtime bytecode is not treated as an application identity; BlurPool and Starknet proxy storage owners are reviewed through verified delegate implementation profiles.",
    "S4 final selector closure adds source-reviewed owner-scoped lifecycle/message selectors only. Read-only Arbitrum bridge counters share the conservative per-bridge singleton dependency through query::ReadRouteLock; XEN claim-and-stake is implemented atomically in the native XEN state machine. Unresolved selectors remain opaque."
  ],
